# Builder Rules

This project creates custom React components for Builder.io publishing.

## Default Behaviour

Unless explicitly overridden, every new component must:
1. Be created using the `create-component` skill
2. Be registered in `builder-registry.ts` using the `register-component` skill
3. Be added to the showcase in `app/showcase/page.tsx` using the `showcase-component` skill

Additionally, header/nav and footer components are automatically wired into the homepage layout (`app/page.tsx`, served at `/`): a hardcoded header, Builder Publish content in the middle, and a hardcoded footer. A component is treated as header/footer by naming convention (name contains `Header`/`NavBar` or `Footer`); every other component stays out of `app/page.tsx` and is Builder-managed content only.

## Overriding Default Behaviour

Opt out by saying:
- "Don't add this to the showcase" → skip step 3
- "Don't register this in builder-registry" → skip step 2
- "This is an internal utility component" → skip steps 2 and 3
- "Don't add this to the homepage layout" → skip wiring it into `app/page.tsx`'s header/footer slot
